{"version":3,"term":{"cols":80,"rows":30,"type":"xterm-256color","version":"xterm.js(6.1.0-beta.285)"},"timestamp":1784555515,"idle_time_limit":3.0,"command":"bash thunderagent-demo.sh","title":"ThunderAgent: Program-Aware Agentic Scheduling in Dynamo","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.016, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\r\n║  ThunderAgent — Program-Aware Agentic Scheduling in Dynamo ║\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\r\n\r\n"]
[2.008, "o", "\u001b[1;37mTHE PROBLEM:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  Agentic LLM workloads (Claude Code, SWE-Agent, OpenHands) work like:\r\n\r\n    LLM call → tool call (pytest, docker, curl) → LLM call → tool call → ...\r\n\r\n  Between LLM turns, the agent runs tools (non-GPU work), but its\r\n  KV cache stays resident on the GPU — wasting memory.\r\n\r\n  Standard routers see each turn independently. They don't know that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  turns belong to the same agent, so they can't:\r\n    • Pin an agent to one worker (for KV cache reuse)\r\n    • Pause idle agents at tool boundaries to free GPU memory\r\n    • Resume them when capacity is available\r\n\r\n"]
[8.020, "o", "\u001b[1;37mTHE SOLUTION — ThunderAgent:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  ThunderAgent groups all turns from one agent into a 'Program' and\r\n  schedules at the program level. Each program has:\r\n\r\n    • Status:    REASONING (LLM active) or ACTING (running tools)\r\n    • Lifecycle: ACTIVE (can submit) or PAUSED (held until memory frees)\r\n\r\n  A background scheduler ticks every 5s with three phases:\r\n    1. Soft-demote: priority penalty in a warning band\r\n    2. Greedy resume: BFD bin-pack smallest paused programs\r\n    3. Pause until safe: park idle programs at tool boundaries\r\n\r\n  Paper: 1.5–3.6× throughput improvement (ICML 2026 Spotlight)\r\n\r\n"]
[8.026, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1;37mARCHITECTURE — Where ThunderAgent fits in Dynamo:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "  │ dynamo.frontend  (HTTP + OpenAI-compatible API)   │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │ Receives chat completions with session headers    │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘\r\n                          │  x-dynamo-session-id\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "                          ▼\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │ dynamo.thunderagent_router  ← THIS SERVICE        │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │                                                   │\r\n  │  • ProgramTable: session_id → program state       │\r\n  │  • Admission gate: pause/resume at tool boundary  │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │  • Sticky worker pin per program                  │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │  • Wraps KvRouter for actual routing decisions    │\r\n  └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────────┘\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "                          │  dispatches to best worker\r\n                          ▼\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\r\n  │ dynamo.vllm  (GPU workers, publish KV events)     │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\r\n\r\n  Key design: ThunderAgent owns a KvRouter in-process (no extra hop).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  Requests without session headers pass through unchanged.\r\n\r\n"]
[10.025, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[1;37mHOW SESSION TRACKING WORKS:\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  Dynamo doesn't auto-detect agentic workloads. It's opt-in via headers:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ┌─────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┐\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │ Agent Framework         │ Session Header                   │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  ├─────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────┤\r\n  │ Generic / any agent     │ x-dynamo-session-id              │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │ Claude Code             │ x-claude-code-session-id         │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  │ Codex                   │ session-id                       │\r\n  │ OpenCode                │ x-session-id                     │\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  └─────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────┘\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  The frontend normalizes these into agent_context.session_id.\r\n  ThunderAgent uses this to create/lookup a Program.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  To end a session: send x-dynamo-session-final: true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  This releases the program from the table and frees resources.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[8.023, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.001, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\r\n║  LIVE DEMO — ThunderAgent on Kubernetes                    ║\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\r\n\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  Deployment: Frontend → ThunderAgentRouter → vLLM Worker\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  Model: Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B on 1x A100 GPU\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  Deployed via Dynamo Graph Deployment (DGD) on the Dynamo Operator\r\n\r\n"]
[4.012, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# Step 1: Deploy ThunderAgent via DGD (Dynamo Graph Deployment)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.014, "o", "\u001b[0;90m  The DGD defines three services: Frontend, ThunderAgentRouter, VllmDecodeWorker.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.014, "o", "\u001b[0;90m  The Dynamo Operator creates pods, configures networking, and mounts the model PVC.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.008, "o", "\u001b[1;32m❯ \u001b[0m"]
