[0.000, "o", "╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "║  Demo Summary                                              ║\r\n╠══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\r\n║                                                            ║\r\n║  What we showed:                                           ║\r\n║  ✓ ThunderAgent deploys as a Dynamo router service         ║\r\n║  ✓ No session header → plain pass-through (compatible)     ║\r\n║  ✓ With session header → program tracking + sticky pin     ║\r\n║  ✓ Multi-turn → same GPU worker (KV cache reuse)          ║\r\n║  ✓ Session final → clean program release                   ║\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "║                                                            ║\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "║  What happens under memory pressure (large model/many      ║\r\n║  agents): ThunderAgent's scheduler pauses idle programs    ║\r\n║  at tool boundaries and resumes them via BFD bin-packing   ║\r\n║  when GPU capacity frees up. This achieves 1.5–3.6×        ║\r\n║  throughput improvement on agentic benchmarks.             ║\r\n║                                                            ║\r\n║  Learn more:                                               ║\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "║  • Paper: arxiv.org/abs/2602.13692 (ICML 2026 Spotlight)  ║\r\n║  • Code: components/src/dynamo/thunderagent_router/        ║\r\n║  • Docs: docs/agents/thunderagent-router.md               ║\r\n║                                                            ║\r\n╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\r\n\r\n"]
